--TEST--
A `var` declaration is the one spelling that hides the type it inferred, so it is the one that gets it back — after the name, where the annotation it did not write would have gone, `rule:types/var-inference` and `rule:ide/every-feature-is-staged-behind-its-dependency`
--FILE--
<?nvs
var $count = 41;
var $greeting = "hi";
--REQUEST--
inlayHint
--EXPECT--
2:11 type : int
3:14 type : string
